---
const features = [
  {
    icon: '\u266B',
    title: 'Library first',
    body: 'Built around your own folders and files, not around pushing you into an online catalog.',
  },
  {
    icon: '\u2913',
    title: 'Downloads that stay coherent',
    body: 'yt-dlp and ffmpeg install together in one step, update checks are real, and the download folder is configurable.',
  },
  {
    icon: '\u25B6',
    title: 'Playback that remembers',
    body: 'Volume, queue, track, and position all survive restarts so you pick up right where you left off.',
  },
  {
    icon: '\u2726',
    title: 'Quiet interface touches',
    body: 'Collapsible sidebar, optional lyrics panel, and a cleaner now playing surface keep the layout relaxed.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section-shell section-stack" id="features">
  <div class="section-heading reveal">
    <div class="pill">What makes it feel like Shiranami</div>
    <h2>Everything is aimed at a calmer listening flow.</h2>
    <p>
      The first release is about removing friction: less reloading, less setup repetition, and fewer
      panels fighting for attention while you listen.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-grid reveal-stagger">
    {features.map((feature) => (
      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{feature.icon}</span>
        <h3>{feature.title}</h3>
        <p>{feature.body}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
